# Python runtime artifacts
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# The global ~/.gitignore ignores all CLAUDE.md files (project-local instructions).
# Our repo-managed global CLAUDE.md is an intentional tracked exception.
!ai/claude/CLAUDE.md

# The global ~/.gitignore also hides `.claude/` and `CLAUDE.md` so that personal
# Claude config stays out of the project repos it is symlinked into. Inside THIS
# repo those files are the payload, not noise, so re-include them. The parent
# directory has to be re-included first — git will not descend into an excluded
# directory to reach a negated file inside it.
!projects/*/.claude/
!projects/*/CLAUDE.md

# ...except host-specific state, which stays local. (Also covered by the global
# ignore; repeated here so this repo is self-explanatory.)
projects/*/.claude/settings.local.json

# Machine-local workspace overrides for the dev platform (host paths, env, and
# anything that must not follow the repo to another machine).
projects/*/workspace.local.yaml
